{"tool_name":"imshot","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"imshot","home":"https://github.com/wasimaftab/ImShot","license":"Other","summary":"The software ImShot aims to identifying peptides obtained in MALDI-IMS.","addition_date":"2022-08-28T12:44:35.048909Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:46:17.207447Z","tool_type":["Desktop application","Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:imshot","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"imhof@lmu.de","name":"Axel Imhof","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"shibojyoti.lahiri@med.uni-muenchen.de","name":"Shibojyoti Lahiri","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Mass spectra calibration","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3627"},{"term":"Protein identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3767"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"ImShot","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100242","metadata":{"abstract":"Imaging mass spectrometry (IMS) has developed into a powerful tool allowing label-free detection of numerous biomolecules in situ. In contrast to shotgun proteomics, proteins/peptides can be detected directly from biological tissues and correlated to its morphology leading to a gain of crucial clinical information. However, direct identification of the detected molecules is currently challenging for MALDI-IMS, thereby compelling researchers to use complementary techniques and resource intensive experimental setups. Despite these strategies, sufficient information could not be extracted because of lack of an optimum data combination strategy/software. Here, we introduce a new open-source software ImShot that aims at identifying peptides obtained in MALDI-IMS. This is achieved by combining information from IMS and shotgun proteomics (LC-MS) measurements of serial sections of the same tissue. The software takes advantage of a twogroup comparison to determine the search space of IMS masses after deisotoping the corresponding spectra. Ambiguity in annotations of IMS peptides is eliminated by introduction of a novel scoring system that identifies the most likely parent protein of a detected peptide in the corresponding IMS dataset. Thanks to its modular structure, the software can also handle LC-MS data separately and display interactive enrichment plots and enriched Gene Ontology terms or cellular pathways. The software has been built as a desktop application with a conveniently designed graphic user interface to provide users with a seamless experience in data analysis. ImShot can run on all the three major desktop operating systems and is freely available under Massachusetts Institute of Technology license.","authors":[{"name":"Aftab W."},{"name":"Imhof A."},{"name":"Lahiri S."}],"citationCount":4,"date":"2022-06-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","title":"ImShot: An Open-Source Software for Probabilistic Identification of Proteins In Situ and Visualization of Proteomics Data"},"pmcid":"PMC9194865","pmid":"35569805"}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ImShot","home":"https://bio.tools/imshot","license":"Other","summary":"The software ImShot aims to identifying peptides obtained in MALDI-IMS.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:imshot/app/github.com","@license":"https://